WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.907
A green n8n run can still address the wrong customer.

00:00:03.927 --> 00:00:13.056
This is n8n Execution Dossier, for agency technical leads who need to review an automation change on the Jira issue where the team already works.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.167
Start with the saved evidence.

00:00:16.187 --> 00:00:22.633
If a required execution is missing, the tool returns its filename and concrete export steps.

00:00:22.653 --> 00:00:30.824
Fetch the complete execution with includeData set to true, take the child ID from the parent's saved call metadata, and attach the file.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.140
Here is the complete synthetic case, KAN-2: original and repaired parent and child exports.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.194
I call the MCP tool with this issue key.

00:00:43.214 --> 00:00:50.032
Forge reads all four attachments as the authenticated Jira user and verifies the actual parent-child call edges.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.470
The original has two mismatches.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:15.067
Returned item zero should trace to input three, customer D, but the parent recorded input zero, customer A. Item one should trace to input two, customer C, but recorded input one, customer B. Each finding gives the attachment ID and exact JSON pointer: the parent

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:19.010
pairing, child terminal pairing, and expected caller input.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:22.048
The repaired saved call agrees for both items.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.734
Open the same issue.

00:01:32.754 --> 00:01:41.381
The tool has left a native Jira comment with the before-and-after counts, matched execution and workflow IDs, and raw-evidence locations.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:45.296
Reviewers can open the original attachments to check the result.

00:01:45.316 --> 00:01:48.212
The customer JSON stays in those files.

00:01:48.232 --> 00:01:51.184
HTTP acceptance remains a separate check.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.985
Run the same audit again.

00:01:58.005 --> 00:02:03.857
It returns reused and the same comment ID, with the invoking user's authorship verified.

00:02:03.877 --> 00:02:07.559
This preserves one case for these attachments and this user.

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:11.048
Replacing an attachment gives the next case its own marker.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.510
To use it, open the public installation link, select your Jira site, and install.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:30.554
A site administrator enables the tool under Connected apps, then you connect this endpoint through Atlassian OAuth in your MCP client.

00:02:30.574 --> 00:02:34.256
Attach your saved executions and supply the issue key.

00:02:34.276 --> 00:02:39.704
The result is a reviewable n8n change case, delivered exactly where the team needs it.

